WEBVTT

00:00:00.726 --> 00:00:02.893
Welcome to the Prac360 support desk.

00:00:02.893 --> 00:00:07.467
This training shows you how to handle practice queries from start to finish:

00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:14.991
tickets, the AI support assistant, phone calls through 3CX, your schedule, automation, and the numbers your manager looks at.

00:00:15.733 --> 00:00:17.805
The Overview is your start screen.

00:00:17.805 --> 00:00:26.701
At the top you see open tickets, what needs attention right now, our average first reply, tickets solved this week, satisfaction and missed calls.

00:00:26.701 --> 00:00:36.268
Just below, the AI support strip shows how many requests the assistant answered, how many it solved without a consultant, and how many it handed to a person.

00:00:38.268 --> 00:00:41.510
Below that is your own queue, and the team right now:

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:47.812
who is available, who is on a call, who is away or on leave, and how many open tickets each person has.

00:00:47.812 --> 00:00:49.464
Missed calls show here too.

00:00:49.464 --> 00:00:51.544
One click calls the practice back.

00:00:52.804 --> 00:00:54.943
Under Tickets you see every query.

00:00:54.943 --> 00:01:03.057
Use the filters for your own tickets, those not assigned yet, those that need attention, AI assisted tickets, or repeat requests.

00:01:03.057 --> 00:01:06.894
Sort by urgency, ticket number, date created or last changed.

00:01:06.894 --> 00:01:09.788
The coloured label is the service level clock:

00:01:09.788 --> 00:01:13.310
green is on time, orange is at risk, and red is overdue.

00:01:15.565 --> 00:01:17.127
Open a ticket to work on it.

00:01:17.127 --> 00:01:23.039
On the right, Live at the practice shows who at that practice is signed in right now, and on which screen.

00:01:23.039 --> 00:01:24.377
Press Connect to screen:

00:01:24.377 --> 00:01:29.062
the reason is filled in for you, and the user must allow it before you see anything.

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:32.615
Below are the details:

00:01:32.615 --> 00:01:39.653
status, consultant, priority and category, with the service level for this priority, and the Touchpoints:

00:01:39.653 --> 00:01:44.680
every message, call, note, assignment and AI step on this ticket, in order.

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:47.830
If it is not yours yet, press Take this ticket.

00:01:51.142 --> 00:01:56.214
To answer the practice, write your reply, choose how long you spent, and what happens next.

00:01:56.214 --> 00:02:00.394
The practice sees your answer straight away in their Client support portal.

00:02:02.621 --> 00:02:05.628
Use an internal note for anything only the team should see.

00:02:05.628 --> 00:02:08.737
Notes are marked in yellow, and the practice never sees them.

00:02:11.621 --> 00:02:13.399
Now the AI support assistant.

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:19.957
Requests that practices log in Client support are answered first by the assistant, usually within a minute.

00:02:19.957 --> 00:02:28.661
It only uses Prac360's own help guides and the claim rules, and it checks the practice's own data, such as rejected claims, before it answers.

00:02:30.165 --> 00:02:33.445
Every answer is marked AI support, so you always know.

00:02:33.445 --> 00:02:36.846
Before anything is sent, seven quality checks must pass:

00:02:36.846 --> 00:02:51.605
it understood the request, it only uses our own help, the screens it points to exist, it is safe for a medical practice with no clinical advice, it is in plain language, it fits the category, and it does not repeat something that did not work.

00:02:53.613 --> 00:02:56.873
The practice presses It is sorted now, or replies.

00:02:56.873 --> 00:03:01.762
If the answer did not help, the assistant tries once more, then hands over.

00:03:01.762 --> 00:03:07.565
To step in yourself, press Take over from the assistant, or simply reply to the practice.

00:03:08.945 --> 00:03:12.111
Anything risky or uncertain goes straight to a person:

00:03:12.111 --> 00:03:20.907
critical problems, phone calls, security, money, missing data, clinical questions, system faults, unhappy practices, and anyone who asks for a person.

00:03:20.907 --> 00:03:26.068
The assistant writes a hand-over note for you, and the ticket is assigned automatically.

00:03:26.068 --> 00:03:31.462
If a practice asks whether they are talking to a person, it answers honestly and hands over.

00:03:33.643 --> 00:03:35.465
It also handles repeat requests.

00:03:35.465 --> 00:03:40.644
A duplicate of an open ticket is combined, and the practice is told which ticket to follow.

00:03:40.644 --> 00:03:46.279
A problem already with development is linked, and the practice gets progress updates automatically.

00:03:46.279 --> 00:03:50.207
And a question asked before gets the answer that solved it last time.

00:03:50.207 --> 00:03:54.476
When it is not sure, you see Possible duplicate, with one click to combine.

00:03:57.589 --> 00:03:59.140
Calls come in through 3CX.

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:04.987
When a practice phones, Prac360 recognises the number and shows the practice and its open tickets.

00:04:04.987 --> 00:04:11.192
Answer, link the call to a ticket, and when you hang up the call and your time are logged on the ticket.

00:04:12.749 --> 00:04:18.756
On the Calls tab you dial out with one click, see every recent call, and connect 3CX:

00:04:18.756 --> 00:04:22.502
add your 3CX address and each consultant's extension.

00:04:22.502 --> 00:04:27.873
For incoming calls, 3CX opens this Prac360 address with the caller's number.

00:04:30.488 --> 00:04:32.235
Some problems need a developer.

00:04:32.235 --> 00:04:33.701
Press Send to development:

00:04:33.701 --> 00:04:37.195
it goes straight to the Bugs and ideas list in the Admin tool.

00:04:37.195 --> 00:04:40.069
From then on the practice is updated automatically:

00:04:40.069 --> 00:04:45.423
when the fix is planned, when it is being built, and when it is fixed, with a request to check.

00:04:47.001 --> 00:04:49.203
Going on leave, or need a specialist?

00:04:49.203 --> 00:04:50.869
Ask the manager to reassign.

00:04:50.869 --> 00:04:57.771
The manager sees all flagged tickets, and those of people on leave, on the Overview, and moves them with one choice.

00:05:00.218 --> 00:05:02.686
The Schedule shows the whole team's week:

00:05:02.686 --> 00:05:06.359
leave, half days, training, projects and after-hours on call.

00:05:06.359 --> 00:05:11.778
Leave waits for the manager's approval, and automatic assignment skips anyone who is away.

00:05:13.473 --> 00:05:16.286
Automation is where you set up the AI assistant:

00:05:16.286 --> 00:05:22.967
on or off, how sure it must be, how many answers before it hands over, and which categories always go to a person.

00:05:22.967 --> 00:05:31.465
Below that, rules send every new ticket to the right team, balanced by how busy each person is, and you set the service levels for each priority.

00:05:33.441 --> 00:05:36.868
KPIs and reports show how each consultant is doing:

00:05:36.868 --> 00:05:43.118
open and solved tickets, first reply, service level met, satisfaction, time logged and calls.

00:05:43.118 --> 00:05:51.920
The AI section shows what the assistant solved, why tickets went to a person, the repeat requests it handled, and every touchpoint.

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:53.869
Export it all with one click.

00:05:56.272 --> 00:05:57.834
Clients is your C.R.M.:

00:05:57.834 --> 00:06:03.945
every practice with its plan, contacts, notes, tickets and calls, and its account manager.

00:06:05.955 --> 00:06:09.287
And this is what the practice sees, in their own Client support portal.

00:06:14.955 --> 00:06:19.875
When we need an answer from the practice, everyone there gets this reminder, with Reply now.

00:06:19.875 --> 00:06:24.206
If they are busy, they can mute it for two hours, and then it reminds them again.

00:06:26.958 --> 00:06:30.745
Under their name, Client support shows all their practice's requests:

00:06:30.745 --> 00:06:35.795
where each one is, and every reply, with Show me how buttons that walk them through the fix.

00:06:35.795 --> 00:06:39.911
They can log a request, ask us to call them, and rate us when it is solved.

00:06:42.612 --> 00:06:44.482
That's the Prac360 support desk:

00:06:44.482 --> 00:06:51.615
the AI assistant answers first, you step in when it matters, every call is logged, and every practice is kept in the loop.

00:06:51.615 --> 00:06:53.661
Thank you, and welcome to the team.

